WEBVTT

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.120
Thank you.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.140
We are a fan.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:22.440
I'll see you.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:30.500
Thank you.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.000
A super future family.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:41.040
A family brought together by faith and given superpowers through the miracle of modern science.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:56.650
So damn it!

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.260
vocabulary.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:29.660
Let's get them.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.010
Port one, the mothership.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:42.650
Uh-oh.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.100
One.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.460
I'm under you.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.320
Let's go.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:01:59.980
No.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.040
Sonic 1?

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.820
Play like an earthling.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.080
All right.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:11.800
Yeah, that's showing them.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:12.360
We did it.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.580
That's showing them.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.240
Not a very good showing, I'm afraid, Sharp.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.170
Why, that's outrageous.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.690
Just what was wrong with the demonstration, Mr. Nudnick?

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.930
They defeated your robots.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.770
Hardly. They destroyed a few simple robotic soldiers.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.540
But the mothership escaped Bionic one was too busy saving sport one to complete the mission

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.620
Well, what did you want me to do, let him die?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.400
Your mission was to stop the mother ship.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.360
You let your human emotions interfere, and you failed.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.360
Now, this would not have happened with our new trionic technology.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:51.910
Try Onyx, shmye Onyx. I'm not going to sacrifice a member of this team in a field test.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.960
You people from Q10 always passing judgment on things you don't understand.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.130
Well, Mother One...

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.810
We're people, not machines!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.060
Their tests aren't fair or accurate. They're based on unrealistic situations.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.500
Our tests don't have to be fair or accurate. They just have to get results.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:13.140
Trionics are too dangerous to implement at this stage, and you have no right...

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.780
Your special projects labs are...

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.260
federally funded as the government's quality control agency, Q10, has every right to judge.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:24.040
You must give the Bionic Six a fair test, something real.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.300
Better calm down, Professor Sharp. You're setting a flower on fire.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.960
Wait, wait, this might be...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.940
just what we're looking for. Computer report.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:34.340
Scarab forces sighted

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.040
in vicinity of the Xenovision theater.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.060
What could Scarab want there?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.480
Only one thing.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.060
The projector lens. It's the largest

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.860
pure silicon lens in the world.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.090
If that is what Scarab wants, we'll stop him.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.830
And I'm going with you.

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.890
What? Can't take along a civilian.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.080
You wanted a fair test under real conditions, didn't you?

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.060
Well, this is it. Let's go.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.870
Very well, but I'm coming, too.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:07.340
I got you a prison because I love you.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.100
You're a prison because I heard over you.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.460
And now, now.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:19.910
Darling, nobody move and we won't have to hurt you.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.490
Stop the film.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:29.740
You people have no taste.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.140
Mechanic, Adamo, get the lens.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.200
Your movie career is over, Glove.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.860
Here's a preview of coming attractions.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.260
The Bionic Six!

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:45.390
Give it up, Glove. Your side's retired.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:51.960
You see what I mean, Mr. Nudnik?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.960
Give them a real crisis and they're outstanding.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:58.410
I'm taking notes sharp. I'll make my decisions later.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.580
Now for you, I.Q.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:09.750
Whoops!

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.780
Come on, you buffoon.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.640
Scarab's waiting for the lens.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:18.300
Hold it right there, you mega creeps!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.560
The only place you're going is the showers.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:21.910
Think so?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.630
But I beg to dip-o.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.660
Come on, Lug Rich.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:29.160
I always wanted a screen test, but this is ridiculous!

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.610
Nick, they saved those people's lives.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.390
What do you think of the Bionic Six now?

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.160
The Bionic Six are a menace.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.720
They failed to stop those villains

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:52.220
and almost caused the deaths of innocent people.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:54.200
What? How can you say?

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.940
If the Bionic Six hadn't shown up,

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.620
these people wouldn't have been in danger.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.960
From here on, I'm taking direct...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.880
of the bionic six you can't do that you have no authority i'm in charge here i have all the

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:22.160
authority i need sharp effective immediately you're fired can't we do something professor

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:28.700
no helen i'm afraid it's official i checked with washington apparently nudnik has all the

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:29.900
authority he claims

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.810
You'll obey orders from Nudnick just as though they were coming from me.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.300
Professor, where will you go?

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:42.680
Me? Oh, I've made a reservation at the Galileo Home for Retired Scientists.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:46.800
Thing of the sort. You'll come and live with us. Isn't that right?

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.530
Oh, no. I'd be putting you out.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.700
Nonsense. You're like a member of the family.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.800
You won't be putting us out. You can have Eric's room.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:07.720
Don't you hear that awful racket?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.680
Yes, I can.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.740
What is the source?

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.570
You are.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:15.950
You're snoring.

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:18.250
Impossible.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.970
I am not programmed for snoring.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:27.440
You're not programmed for sleeping either.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.530
Oh, it's not fair.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:38.120
to give up my room and sleep with a robot you don't have to get birds birds personal

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:50.320
were you using my porta tape again what no i what happened to my recording of the unliving

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:57.540
poobahs concert discs are nothing but gibberish oh my dear i'm so sorry i i needed to dictate

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.860
I made some notes and couldn't find my recorder.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.900
I didn't realize you were saving those, uh, sounds.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.860
Sound was ultra-cool rock and roll.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.590
Really? It never dawned on me.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.930
