00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:17.950
I've got a lovely octophonic recording of a harpsichord concerto by Mozart.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.850
That's all right, Professor. Never mind.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:27.220
If he doesn't hurry up, it'll be tomorrow.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:29.810
Yeah, what's taking him so long?

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:34.080
First, he wrecked all the other bathrooms with his plumbing experiment, and now this.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.870
Morning, gang. What's going on?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.290
I thought we had a schedule to prevent this from happening.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.800
Talk to our star boarder.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:42.960
I see.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:49.210
Professor, I think we need to have a little talk.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:50.590
Yes, Jack?

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:51.830
I was just finishing up.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.390
I figured out where I went wrong with the plumbing system.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.230
A few little adjustments, and great.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:56.850
My turn.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:06.930
Looks like we're wanted by Nudnick the Nasty.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.550
Hold on a second, Bungie.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.950
I think we ought to bionicize before we answer.

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:12.330
For security reasons.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:13.970
Just to be on the safe side.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:15.200
Bionicize!

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.500
Let's see what Mr. Nudnick wants.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.520
Bionic 1 online.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.020
18.7 seconds.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.440
Very poor response time, Bionic 6.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.120
Sorry, Mr. Nudnick.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.590
We were changing.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.890
Another flaw in Bionic technology.

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:48.130
When we have our Trionic heroes in place,

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.110
things will be much more efficient.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.180
Did you have an assignment for us, Mr. Nudnick?

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:54.680
Of course, Bionic 1.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.360
This is not a social call.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.020
You're to split up into teams.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.960
I've programmed the coordinates into your...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.170
computer. These assignments should be within your limited bionic abilities. Is it Scarab? Your

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:17.770
assignments will be obvious when you arrive. Ludnik offline. Stop! For this, we're bionic.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.250
Saving a kitty.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:33.370
Some job for a superhero.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:37.240
I think you had the right idea, Karate One.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.480
We'll register a complaint with Q10.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:43.340
Right. I'm not going Bionic just to do Nudnick's dumb jobs.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:46.180
That's funny. No lights.

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:49.940
Maybe it's more of Nudnick's efficiency program.

00:10:58.410 --> 00:10:59.250
Mr. Nudnick?

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.720
anybody here? Mr. Nudnick?

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.280
This doesn't make sense, Karate One.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.220
There's a couple of days worth of dust here.

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:13.750
It looks like nobody's used the lab since the professor

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:15.750
moved out. That's impossible.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.730
Where are all the Q10 people?

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.230
And where's all that new trionic technology?

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:22.080
And where's Nudnick?

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:24.640
You have no cause to be upset.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:26.820
I simply sent you on missions

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.640
I was certain you could handle without

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.900
causing danger to yourself.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.770
or the general population.

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:36.610
My technicians are perfecting the first generation of trionic heroes even now.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:40.700
You've made reference to this trionic technology before, Mr. Knudnick.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.560
Just what is it supposed to be?

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.370
Hey, guys, guess what we just found?

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:46.050
Wait!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.380
Huh? The next generation of superheroes, of course.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:55.080
All mechanized and computerized beings with incredible powers

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.800
and without human frailty.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.400
That's not possible.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:11:59.980
Oh, but it is my op...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.260
Obsolete little friend. I'm afraid you'll all soon be joining Sharp in retirement.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:05.520
Nudnik offline.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.740
I didn't mean Trionics were impossible, Bionic One.

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:12.100
What I meant was IQ and I just got back from the SPL.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.500
And it was deserted.

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:18.890
Gotta keep them fretting for a while.

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:24.330
Oh, hail myself.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:28.140
Oh, how I hate tweed suits.

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:29.420
The Matamo Report.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.490
We're making excellent progress, darling.

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:37.210
Thanks to your brother's equipment, we are creating a new generation of Sifrons.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:43.760
A generation more sophisticated, more powerful than anything the Bionic Six have ever faced.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:44.700
Excellent.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:54.400
Excellent! With the new Sifrons and the Bionic Six working under my orders, the world is mine!

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:03.870
Well, Bionic 1, what do you say?

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:07.030
I think it's time we fill them in on the whole story, Professor.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:09.790
Is this some kind of a conspiracy between you two?

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:11.820
What's going on here?

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:14.360
Why did the SPL look abandoned when we were there?

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:17.660
And how could it be busy again when Nudnik called?

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:20.040
Hold on, hold on, one at a time.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:22.510
I think it's best if we start at the very beginning.

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:29.700
Well, it all began some weeks ago when I received a top priority video call from the President of the United States.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.480
He had a special task for me to perform.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:36.770
Care, careful.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:37.650
Careful.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.900
That lens is irreplaceable.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:45.000
Eat, clumsy oafs.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:45.800
Don't drop it.

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.390
Who you calling clumsy?

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:50.810
All right, you two.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:52.350
This isn't romper room.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.310
We've got work to do.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:57.060
Move the siphrons in front of the lens.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:57.580
Hurry.

00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.410
It's a long night ahead of us.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.580
Bring your Super Cypheron forward.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:07.310
Here you are, Scarab, the first of the new breed of Scyphrons.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:08.510
Excellent.

00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:12.230
Now we shall focus my dear brother's energy rays

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:15.230
through the perfect optics of the Xenovision lens

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.910
and triple the power of the Scyphrons.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:20.790
Thank you.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:22.590
Yes, yes.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.590
Well, Scarab.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.040
What's wrong with your tryonics?

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:29.800
Yeah.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.970
What? He's just sitting there.

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.130
Quiet, you fools. Watch.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:37.660
He's alive. Yes, he's alive.

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.540
Well, sort of.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.580
Quickly, another siphon.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.220
And then another, and another.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.480
We've work to do.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.040
A world to conquer.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.700
It's the dawn of a new age.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.960
Think of it, my children.

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:59.780
This handful of cyprons are as strong, as destructive as an entire battalion.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.020
of the former model.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:10.240
We can hardly wait to see these new Siphrons beat the Bionic Six in an unfair fight.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:14.910
That's the only kind of fight your kind can ever win, Chopper.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.130
You're about to become obsolete.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:18.820
Bionic 6.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.860
who are posing as Nudnick all along.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:29.790
no good nick quite humorous karate one we are amused now laugh

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.780
this off. Cybron's

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:32.450
attack.

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:49.240
These things are

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:49.700
strong.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:53.480
And smart.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:59.980
Port one. My ESP.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.320
It tells me these machines have awesome new powers.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:09.240
My eye!

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:14.260
What? What? Look out!

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:22.640
Glove!

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:24.720
Chopper mechanic clunk! Get them!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:27.130
IQ, watch out!

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:37.800
Right, mother one. Nice shooting.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:44.260
Chain letter for your bionic boy.

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:50.860
Kentar.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:17.670
those bionic members get the upper hand they've destroyed all your new cyphrons darling

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.670
Self-destruct program implemented.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.690
60 seconds to self-destruct.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:43.720
59, 58, 57...

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:46.980
I think it's time for a strategic retreat, darling.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:48.940
Reacts on suggestions, my dear.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.000
At least we've destroyed my brother's special project lab.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.540
Come on, kiddies. Let's get out of here.

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:57.640
We can't save the lab. Everybody out.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:13.820
We should be safe from the last year, but when the Bionic Six come out, we'll be waiting.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:18.710
Where are those Bionic buffoons? They don't get out soon, they'll be blown up.

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:20.740
Would that be so bad, darling?

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:29.760
The SPL. Modest music to my ears. The end of the Bionic Six. They're out of my hair.

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:35.400
We're going to be in your hair for a long time to come.

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:37.820
Looks like his hair needs washing to me.

00:18:38.120 --> 00:18:39.220
What do you think, Karate One?

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:41.600
I don't think he has enough hair to wash.

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:44.770
But his clothes look pretty grimy.

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:46.250
Allow me, Scarab.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.700
I already took a bath this year.

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:09.690
Let's get out of here.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:11.310
Before they make us complain.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.740
